  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening TB control in Kosovo - Kosovo (01-Jan-2019-31-Dec-2021)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Kosovo, Tuberculosis, Community Development Fund (CDF)This program has the following goals: To reduce the overall incidence of notified cases from 40.6 per 100,000 in 2017 to 34 per 100,000 in 2021 and maintain tuberculosis mortality in Kosovo below 2/100,000.. The objectives of this program are: Successfully treat all cases of tuberculosis and maintain at least 85% the treatment success rate..  Strengthen the early prevention and detection of tuberculosis by intensifying the active and passive findings of the cases by providing quality services and adequate measures of infection control and LTBI treatment of cases and other ongoing support..  Establish and support national-level policies and legal framework and ensure greater government political and financial commitment to effective TB response in Kosovo.  Improving patient-centred tuberculosis care through increased CSO engagement and strengthening public-private partnership.  Improve national capacity to investigate and assess the impact of tuberculosis control and pre-elimination of interventions.</narrative>
  </description>
